"Pressing “Move to Trash” twice no longer says the first removal failed. The files had already gone, and in Disk the folders that had left were still drawn on the ring." = "Pressing “Move to Trash” twice no longer says the first removal failed. The files had already gone, and in Disk the folders that had left were still drawn on the ring.";
"The Uninstaller counts a file removed together with the folder it was in. The file did go to the Trash — it was only missing from the report, so a removal of four things said three." = "The Uninstaller counts a file removed together with the folder it was in. The file did go to the Trash — it was only missing from the report, so a removal of four things said three.";
"The Uninstaller no longer overstates how much a removal moved to the Trash: two names for one file were counted as two files." = "The Uninstaller no longer overstates how much a removal moved to the Trash: two names for one file were counted as two files.";
"Removing an app that is still running waits for it to quit. Helm used to move the bundle anyway, so a slow app carried on and wrote its settings back on the way out — putting back the leftovers that had just been taken." = "Removing an app that is still running waits for it to quit. Helm used to move the bundle anyway, so a slow app carried on and wrote its settings back on the way out — putting back the leftovers that had just been taken.";
"A switch no longer shows “off” for a module that is already running." = "A switch no longer shows “off” for a module that is already running.";
"The Homebrew console keeps the last thousand lines instead of every line it has ever printed." = "The Homebrew console keeps the last thousand lines instead of every line it has ever printed.";
"Clearing Caches works now — it could never be carried out before. The contents are cleared and the folder stays, in one row and one press as before. Whatever a running app is holding on to stays with it, listed by name, and the row shrinks to what is left." = "Clearing Caches works now — it could never be carried out before. The contents are cleared and the folder stays, in one row and one press as before. Whatever a running app is holding on to stays with it, listed by name, and the row shrinks to what is left.";
"“Show in Finder” opens the folder a file was in when the file itself is gone, and brings Finder forward. It sits beside a file that would not move, beside something Autopilot moved, beside a leftover deleted a moment ago — and in all but one of those places, pressing it did nothing." = "“Show in Finder” opens the folder a file was in when the file itself is gone, and brings Finder forward. It sits beside a file that would not move, beside something Autopilot moved, beside a leftover deleted a moment ago — and in all but one of those places, pressing it did nothing.";
"The sidebar is yours to arrange. Settings → Settings → Sidebar: press Edit and drag a module anywhere — including into a section you made and named yourself. Delete a section and its modules go to the neighbour, never into nothing; “Restore defaults” puts back the arrangement Helm arrived with. The window and the menu-bar icon show the same arrangement, and it survives a restart and an update." = "The sidebar is yours to arrange. Settings → Settings → Sidebar: press Edit and drag a module anywhere — including into a section you made and named yourself. Delete a section and its modules go to the neighbour, never into nothing; “Restore defaults” puts back the arrangement Helm arrived with. The window and the menu-bar icon show the same arrangement, and it survives a restart and an update.";
"Small tidying in Settings. Rows in the Uninstaller are all one height — the “System” mark is a tag beside the name instead of a third line. Login Items no longer says the same thing in two stacked bars. And every size, count and version in the app is in the one typeface Helm keeps for figures." = "Small tidying in Settings. Rows in the Uninstaller are all one height — the “System” mark is a tag beside the name instead of a third line. Login Items no longer says the same thing in two stacked bars. And every size, count and version in the app is in the one typeface Helm keeps for figures.";
"Drag an app to the Trash and Helm offers to clear up after it, a second later — once you switch it on under Uninstaller → Leftovers. The app stays where you put it, and Helm lists the settings, caches and support files it left behind, already ticked; anything matched only by the app’s name arrives unticked. Say no and it does not ask about that app again." = "Drag an app to the Trash and Helm offers to clear up after it, a second later — once you switch it on under Uninstaller → Leftovers. The app stays where you put it, and Helm lists the settings, caches and support files it left behind, already ticked; anything matched only by the app’s name arrives unticked. Say no and it does not ask about that app again.";
"The welcome tour lets you pick what you want. Each module’s screen carries a switch, so you can keep or drop it while you are being introduced to it — and the opening screen asks whether Helm should start with your Mac. The switch starts where the module already stood, so skipping the tour changes nothing." = "The welcome tour lets you pick what you want. Each module’s screen carries a switch, so you can keep or drop it while you are being introduced to it — and the opening screen asks whether Helm should start with your Mac. The switch starts where the module already stood, so skipping the tour changes nothing.";
"Helm no longer asks for permissions the moment you install it. It used to request Full Disk Access and Accessibility on the very first launch, before you had asked it to do anything. Each module now asks for what it needs on its own page, when it needs it." = "Helm no longer asks for permissions the moment you install it. It used to request Full Disk Access and Accessibility on the very first launch, before you had asked it to do anything. Each module now asks for what it needs on its own page, when it needs it.";
